ouped","confidence":0.833,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-102-37"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6091006","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a4f1b92ca715c50127383cdc81615f2fa48237d2603df87423ba00122094eb98","compact":"41ddf98a9c19ff7ba71970161e932da84d0df2d805ef1aac2a6bed5f63c0cbb6","nasal":"41ddf98a9c19ff7ba71970161e932da84d0df2d805ef1aac2a6bed5f63c0cbb6"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-91-7","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":91,"verse":7,"english":"As they looked on the mighty encounter, the celestials and the Asuras, who had come to the conflict, from feeling of regard,* Cheerfully spoke (these words). *i.e. each party out of regard for the warrior to whom it wished well.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-102-38"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6091007","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"15e4c728fe214c760079b76daab85f5b26e443650d365b552ccda6d27d15108f","compact":"a620075d8489957656402c1f3195b7940f56f178da813d859a29ba991cd71204","nasal":"a620075d8489957656402c1f3195b7940f56f178da813d859a29ba991cd71204"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-91-8","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":91,"verse":8,"english":"The Asuras staying there said to the Tennecked one, Be victorious and the celestials again and again said to Rāma, 'Be victorious'!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-102-39"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6091008","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7dc39d4fe862453d4a01c60b46a2d48f9366bb59b6c51b220d287969fe8856d7","compact":"a10764f920f59461b96721ae759d977277c397e20da2ad788b463b7800d1e7b1","nasal":"a10764f920f59461b96721ae759d977277c397e20da2ad788b463b7800d1e7b1"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-91-9","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":91,"verse":9,"english":"In the meantime, the impious Rāvaņa, desirous of slaying Rāghava, from wrath took up a mighty weapon, fraught with the essence of the thunder bolt; sending terrible sounds; capable of destroying all foes-furnished with forks resembling mountain-peaks; tending to strike terror to mind and sight; sharp-pointed resembling the smoking fire rise at the hour of universal dissolution; exceedingly terrible; irresistible (in battle); unbearable even by the Destroyer-the terror of all creatures-terrific; and competent to rive (all things). Flaming up with wrath, Ravana took this dart.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.882,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-102-40"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6091009","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bd0a515b3127e39883e4011e471c7f06d1f8865d393378a86946ed4f807c9f8c","compact":"b19be5d363f52c4f936bfb0f41e9c7ef548148e24258ee1a21aabcc79af3a3c2","nasal":"56bc5be29032356727019810ed2b300b0dca80d86d7c06ce0eba3b5ea345fd32"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-91-10","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":91,"verse":10,"english":"In the meantime, the impious Rāvaņa, desirous of slaying Rāghava, from wrath took up a mighty weapon, fraught with the essence of the thunder bolt; sending terrible sounds; capable of destroying all foes-furnished with forks resembling mountain-peaks; tending to strike terror to mind and sight; sharp-pointed resembling the smoking fire rise at the hour of universal dissolution; exceedingly terrible; irresistible (in battle); unbearable even by the Destroyer-the terror of all creatures-terrific; and competent to rive (all things). Flaming up with wrath, Ravana took this dart.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.694,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-102-40"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6091010","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEditi