c Rāghava hit (Rāvaņa) in the temples with three feathered shafts.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.833,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-102-56"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6091028","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d35228983fd885ee01177b96d08dde1b7fc0fcbac33d395a9d03c5375197f7df","compact":"5fc6e5aa414c9fae20e40f6ba76588754fb13b0c352a459ea43015727486ae98","nasal":"5fc6e5aa414c9fae20e40f6ba76588754fb13b0c352a459ea43015727486ae98"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-91-29","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":91,"verse":29,"english":"Thereat with all his limbs pierced (with arrows), and his body laved in blood, the lord of Räkşasas furnished with many limbs, looked like a flowering Asoka.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.647,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-102-57"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6091029","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"092366be10a11f5c65275dec4fff5c868b2b0db6384aa817140bfddc891d0fd9","compact":"8a4c65fc0aa86decb65092ad47c23940149013afbe71bd4c9fa9d40a6c8bfe5b","nasal":"bfc3c95c18f00678e198990cd8d21406dca4a3a3eedc1ee65747611c38b05d17"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-91-30","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":91,"verse":30,"english":"With his person pierced with the shafts of Rāma, the lord of night-rangers having his body drenched with blood, was stricken with sadness in the midst of his forces, and was also overwhelmed with terrific wrath.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-102-58"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6091030","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9b80e4c7481711b5f1b805fee307fac39e9ddf13cc6b2e2ae51f406a638259cc","compact":"d8f451a8545cf332410a600dd4ac6b1e22f2daed06014fa175b3b1072f8f1813","nasal"